EXT. SUDS CITY CAR WASH - NIGHT

Neon blue. Wet concrete. A tunnel of spinning brushes humming in the dark. An empty lot beyond.

INT. CAR WASH OFFICE - CONTINUOUS

A closet with a space heater, a cracked radio, a wall of keys. DESHAWN MCALLISTER (18, graduation gown unzipped over a polo, name tag reading "DESHAWN") counts out a till. LUCIA FERREIRA-KANG (18, same gown, mascara smudged) perches on a stool, shoes in her lap.

LUCIA
You work here every Friday?

DESHAWN
Every night.

LUCIA
Even tonight?

DESHAWN
Especially.

Lucia turns the radio dial. Static, then a slow song. She leaves it.

LUCIA
They called your name.

DESHAWN
I know. I was there.

LUCIA
I mean it was loud. Your section.

DESHAWN
My mom brought the airhorn.

LUCIA
Of course she did.

He nearly smiles. Folds the till into a canvas bag.

LUCIA (CONT'D)
My dad didn't come.

DESHAWN
I'm sorry.

LUCIA
It's fine.

DESHAWN
It's not.

LUCIA
No. It's not.

She looks at the shoes in her lap. He busies himself with the keys.

DESHAWN
You hungry?

LUCIA
I could eat.

DESHAWN
There's a place by the freeway. Pancakes.

LUCIA
It's eleven p.m.

DESHAWN
That's when they're best.

A knock. They both turn.

MR. OBUYA (60s, owner, windbreaker, flashlight) leans in the doorway.

MR. OBUYA
Deshawn. Why is the tunnel still running?

DESHAWN
I thought you wanted it warm.

MR. OBUYA
I wanted it empty. Shut it down.

DESHAWN
Yes, sir.

Mr. Obuya looks at Lucia. At the gown. At the shoes.

MR. OBUYA
Congratulations.

LUCIA
Thank you.

MR. OBUYA
Both of you.

He goes. Deshawn exhales. Lucia unfolds from the stool.

LUCIA
Would you get fired?

DESHAWN
Probably not.

LUCIA
But you'd tell me if you would.

DESHAWN
No.

She laughs, shaky. He holds the door. They step into the neon and the tunnel hums, spinning for nobody.

EXT. CAR WASH LOT - CONTINUOUS

Deshawn hits a breaker. The brushes slow. Stop. The silence is enormous.

LUCIA
That was loud.

DESHAWN
That was nothing.

She shrugs off her gown and drapes it on the hood of a stranger's car. Hers, her father's idea of a car, a long dead sedan. After a moment, he does the same.

LUCIA
Pancakes.

DESHAWN
Pancakes.

They walk toward the road. Behind them, the neon buzzes and goes out.
